              <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="230" resized="false" width="180" x="454" y="184">calculation follows a fixed-point technique, an iterative approach where tags are initialized with an initial value and repeatedly updated until the delta reaches the minimum threshold&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P:PI imputed and inferred tag imputed data&lt;br&gt;O/P: Current data of tags</description>
              <description align="center" color="green" colored="true" height="467" resized="true" width="241" x="648" y="10"/>
              <description align="center" color="transparent" colored="true" height="285" resized="true" width="229" x="662" y="189">PEEO-optimized data is retrieved and used to calculate inferred tags, which are stored as peeo_optimum_data for SEEC calculation. A comparison with actual values is made, followed by data adjustment for variable tags, which are saved in adjusted_tags_mapping for further processing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;I/P:PI Current data&lt;br&gt;O/P: Current data&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Stored:&lt;br&gt;1. peeo_optimum_data&lt;br&gt;2. adjusted_actual_value</description>
            </process>
