      <description align="center" color="red" colored="true" height="732" resized="true" width="280" x="16" y="30">Energy Optimizer&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Author&lt;br&gt;Naveen Kumar&lt;br&gt;Karthik Sanagapalli&lt;br&gt;Sai Siva Pedapalem&lt;br&gt;Akshay Hasabe&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Energy Optimization Model is a real-time system that minimizes energy costs while meeting the demands of various users, such as plants and assets. Using the Python GEKKO solver, it determines optimal operating conditions for the utility plant.&lt;br&gt;The model compares current operations with these optimal conditions, identifying inefficiencies and suggesting actionable adjustments. By enabling continuous monitoring and real-time feedback, it ensures maximum efficiency and adaptability to changing conditions.</description>
